OpenSSL 4.1 support for ext/openssl (php-5.4)

OpenSSL 4.1 made ASN1_STRING opaque (str->data / str->length no longer
compile), removed ASN1_STRING_data() and deprecated ASN1_STRING_length().
The version specific SSL methods are gone as well and the ones that remain
return const SSL_METHOD *.

 - str->data / ASN1_STRING_data(x)       -> ASN1_STRING_get0_data(x)
 - str->length / ASN1_STRING_length(x)   -> ASN1_STRING_get_length(x)
 - TLSv1_client_method()/server_method() -> TLS_method()/TLS_server_method()
 - SSL_METHOD *method                    -> const SSL_METHOD *method

The accessors go through php_ASN1_STRING_* macros, so the code still builds
against OpenSSL 3.x.

Patch against upstream php-5.4.45 sources, on top of 00210/00230/00250.

--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
